<title>BELGIUM: Tractebel, Powerfin to merge.</title>
<headline>Tractebel, Powerfin to merge.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian utility Tractebel is planning to merge with its Powerfin unit, offering one new Tractebel share for three Powerfin shares, the companies said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Tractebel is a unit of Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB), itself a unit of French Cie de Suez.</p>
<p>Tractebel currently has about 60 percent of Powerfin, its international energy unit.  </p>
<p>Tractebel said in a statement that the exchange ratio offered was fair for both Tractebel and Powerfin shareholders. The offer had been reviewed by three financial institutions.</p>
<p>The reasons for the merger were:</p>
<p>- simplification of field operations;</p>
<p>- reduction of overhead costs;</p>
<p>- tax related savings;</p>
<p>- a clearer group image;</p>
<p>- avoidance of potential conflicts of interests; and</p>
<p>- an increase of market liquidity in the shares.</p>
</text>
